From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro: disable CQE on the eMMC

With the command queue engine the RG Vita Pro eMMC (G1J9R8, HS400
enhanced strobe) logs cqhci "spurious TCN" and "Failed to halt" CQE
recoveries from the first seconds of boot. Writes then stall, the
desktop freezes when left alone, and btrfs on the eMMC picks up
corruption. The Armbian RG Vita Pro DTS drops supports-cqe for the same
reason, and plain mode is stable there at full speed.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts
@@ -1201,6 +1201,12 @@
 	non-removable;
 	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
 	mmc-hs400-enhanced-strobe;
+	/*
+	 * CQE breaks on this eMMC: cqhci "spurious TCN" and "Failed to halt"
+	 * recovery loops from boot onwards, I/O stalls under sustained writes
+	 * and btrfs corruption. Plain (non-CQ) mode is stable at full speed.
+	 */
+	/delete-property/ supports-cqe;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
